{
  "name": "Cryptojacking in Forgotten K8s Pod",
  "description": "A 'temporary' debug pod from a 2023 hackathon was left running with the cluster-admin token mounted and the kube-api on a public NodePort. Crawlers find it, drop xmrig, and start mining Monero. CPU on three nodes pegs to 100% and pricing-svc latency spikes.",
  "reasoning": "The compromise lives on a side pod ('debug-shell') that shares a node with the pricing-svc replicas. The simulation models pricing-svc as 'degraded' due to noisy-neighbour CPU, and the debug-shell pod itself as 'compromised'.",
